\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RINDEFmodposs
\item[* relevant examples:]
\item[* language:]  English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule)
\item[* subgrammar:] NP-subgrammar
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) (NP)modpossrules
\item[* date of creation:] 21-JUN-1988 16:44:35  
\item[* author:] Franciska de Jong
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 28/10/88\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo
\item date: 24/07/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Margreet Sanders\\
Replaced `complrel' by `objrel' in the PREPP
\item date: 31/07/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Margreet Sanders\\
Copied superdeixis for NPrec2 from NPrec1 (iso CNrec1) in analysis\\
Added reset of cases and genericity (cf. CNmodposs);\\
adapted default persprocase (subrule 3): omegacase, not nominative.
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] 
Introduction of postnominal possessive `of'-modifiers as modifier of an NP
with head/INDEFPRO \\ \\
  A1 in SUBRULE 3 : I $\rightarrow$ me, we $\rightarrow$ us, etc.,
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] cf. CNmodposs3
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\
PERSPRO's, WHPRO's, INDEFPRO's, PROPERNOUNs and EN's are not dominated by CN 
\end{enumerate}
