\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE RNPapposition (* conditions probably must be sharpened  *)

< m1: NP{NPrec1}[mu1] 
  m2: NP{NPrec2}[mu2] 
>

< m : NP{NPrec3}[head/NP{NPrec1}[mu1],
                 puncrel/PUNC(KEY_commaPUNCkey){PUNCrec1},
                 apposrel/NP{NPrec4}[mu4],
                 I1:sig1
                ]
>



   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: ALL(sig1, puncrel/PUNC(KEY_commaPUNCkey){PUNCrec2})
      >

<
   SUBRULE
      < >
      < sig1: [puncrel/PUNC(KEY_commaPUNCkey){PUNCrec3}]>

   (* No COMP *)

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: NPrec1.number = NPrec4.number AND
              NPrec1.cases = NPrec4.cases AND
              NPrec1.mood = nowh AND
              NPrec1.mood = NPrec4.mood AND
              NPrec1.NPhead IN [persproNP, othernp] AND
              NPrec4.NPhead IN [ othernp] AND
              NPrec4.generic = omegageneric AND
              NPrec4.cases = NPrec1.cases

          A1: NPrec1 := NPrec3;
              QUOTE_assigncase(NPrec4,mu4,NPrec2,mu2,[]); 
              NPrec2.superdeixis := NPrec1.superdeixis;
              NPrec2.generic := nogeneric;
         >

   SUBRULE
      < >
      < sig1: []>

      COMP
         <
          C1: NPrec1.number = NPrec2.number AND
              NPrec1.superdeixis = NPrec2.superdeixis AND
              NPrec1.cases = NPrec2.cases AND
              NPrec1.mood = nowh AND
              NPrec1.mood = NPrec2.mood AND
              NPrec1.NPhead IN [persproNP, othernp] AND
              NPrec2.NPhead IN [ othernp] AND
              NPrec2.generic = nogeneric AND
              NPrec2.cases = []

          A1: NPrec3 := NPrec1;
              NPrec4 := NPrec2;
              NPrec4.generic:= omegageneric;
              QUOTE_assigncase(NPrec2,mu2,NPrec4, mu4, NPrec1.cases);
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: NPrec1.number = NPrec4.number AND
              NPrec1.cases = NPrec4.cases AND
              NPrec1.mood = nowh AND
              NPrec1.mood = NPrec4.mood AND
              NPrec1.NPhead IN [persproNP, othernp] AND
              NPrec4.NPhead IN [ othernp] AND
              NPrec4.generic = omegageneric AND
              NPrec4.cases = NPrec1.cases

          A1: NPrec1 := NPrec3;
              QUOTE_assigncase(NPrec4,mu4,NPrec2,mu2,[]); 
              NPrec2.superdeixis := NPrec1.superdeixis;
              NPrec2.generic := nogeneric;
         >


>
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RNPapposition
\item[* relevant examples:] John, my neighbour
\item[* language:] English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] 
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class)
\item[* date of creation:] 2-JAN-1989 17:54:13  
\item[* author:] Franciska de Jong
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 11/12/93\ \ \ \ \ author: Jan Odijk
A Case-Assignemnet statement added, to avoid a crash.
persproNP removed from appositional NPs: if possible at all, they will fail because of Case.
If the appositive NP agrees in Case with the head, then the procedure QUOTE_AssignCase should be adapted.
If it has its own independent Case, then this Case must be assigned here.
This can be tested only with pronouns which distinguish Case:
personal pronouns, wh-pronouns, but these can not occur as appositions. 
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To insert an appostional NP into the NP structure.
